    "greaterDepth": [
      {
        "question": "1a",
        "answer": "4,007 = 4,000 + 0 + 0 + 7; 4,070 = 4,000 + 0 + 70 + 0; 4,700 = 4,000 + 700 + 0 + 0; 7,004 = 7,000 + 0 + 0 + 4; 7,040 = 7,000 + 0 + 40 + 0; 7,400 = 7,000 + 400 + 0 + 0."
      },
      {
        "question": "1b",
        "answer": "Only 4 or 7 can go in the thousands column, because a number starting with 0 is not a 4-digit number. Whichever is there, the other digit can sit in the hundreds, tens or ones, and the two zeros fill the rest. 2 x 3 = 6."
      }
